(7415831, 1169336, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by train:</b></div><hr/><i> Hi Christopher <br/>Excellent work and amazing ideas but I do have to ask you do you have a life outside DPC?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sally, thank you so much for you very kind comment, much appreciated!<br/>In fact DPC (and photography in general) is a rather small part of my life, it is just a hobby, that adds some fun on top of an already very full calendar. It is one of the reasons I don''t enter many challenges: I can pick one week from time to time during which I don''t sleep much, but I wouldn''t be able to do it permanently. Regarding my images, I upload them to several websites (the usual ones: <a href="https://1x.com/member/christophekiciak" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">1X</a>, <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/gyaban_fr/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Flickr</a>, <a href="//gyaban.deviantart.com/gallery/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Deviantart</a>, <a href="https://500px.com/gyaban" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">500px</a>, and <a href="//www.kiciak.fr/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">my own</a>), and sometimes enter other challenges with them, but I didn''t create any book so far (even if my stuff has been included in several ones). Regarding your other questions, I took 1545 photos for this project, but it isn''t very relevant: most are small variations of the same thing, so that I can cherry pick the best ones for each part (for example, 672 alone have been taken during my trip at the sea, because I wanted to be sure to have the appropriate waves pictures, but only 13 were actually used). As for the models, yes, they have been very kind to accept posing for this! However, I''ll probably won''t ask them to do it very often, because I also like to create images with more personal concepts, and I would be uncomfortable dragging someone else into them. Thanks again!</td>', 'Originally posted by train: Hi Christopher Excellent work and amazing ideas but I do have to ask you do you have a life outside DPC?  Sally, thank you so much for you very kind comment, much appreciated!In fact DPC (and photography in general) is a rather small part of my life, it is just a hobby, that adds some fun on top of an already very full calendar. It is one of the reasons I don''t enter many challenges: I can pick one week from time to time during which I don''t sleep much, but I wouldn''t be able to do it permanently. Regarding my images, I upload them to several websites (the usual ones: 1X, Flickr, Deviantart, 500px, and my own), and sometimes enter other challenges with them, but I didn''t create any book so far (even if my stuff has been included in several ones). Regarding your other questions, I took 1545 photos for this project, but it isn''t very relevant: most are small variations of the same thing, so that I can cherry pick the best ones for each part (for example, 672 alone have been taken during my trip at the sea, because I wanted to be sure to have the appropriate waves pictures, but only 13 were actually used). As for the models, yes, they have been very kind to accept posing for this! However, I''ll probably won''t ask them to do it very often, because I also like to create images with more personal concepts, and I would be uncomfortable dragging someone else into them. Thanks again!', '2015-11-12 01:26:09.000000', NULL, 0),
